# Security rules

Apply threat-aware review to security-sensitive changes.

Check where relevant:
- authentication;
- authorization and IDOR;
- privilege escalation;
- injection;
- XSS;
- CSRF;
- SSRF;
- path traversal;
- unsafe file uploads;
- command execution;
- secret leakage;
- sensitive logging;
- insecure defaults;
- replay attacks;
- webhook authenticity;
- rate limiting;
- data exposure;
- mass assignment;
- session and token lifecycle.

Security controls must not be disabled simply to unblock development.
